{"t": 1794110111.8960257, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_or_update_file", "args": {"branch": "eng-91", "content": "\"\"\"HTTP header helpers for the public API.\"\"\"\n\nMIGRATION_URL = \"https://developer.acme.example/migrate\"\n\n\ndef deprecation_headers(sunset_date: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Return the headers that mark an endpoint as deprecated.\n\n    ``sunset_date`` must be an HTTP-date (RFC 7231) string, for example\n    ``\"Wed, 01 Jul 2026 00:00:00 GMT\"``. The headers emitted follow the\n    Deprecation section of the API guidelines.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"Deprecation\": \"true\",\n        \"Sunset\": sunset_date,\n        \"Link\": f'<{MIGRATION_URL}>; rel=\"deprecation\"',\n    }\n", "message": "ENG-91: add deprecation headers helper", "owner": "acme", "path": "api/headers.py", "repo": "public-api"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794110113.692718, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Implements `api.headers.deprecation_headers(sunset_date)` as described in ENG-91.\n\nHeaders follow the Deprecation section of the API guidelines (Notion \u2192 API guidelines):\n\n- `Deprecation: true`\n- `Sunset: <HTTP-date>`\n- `Link: <https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"`\n\nThe caller passes the sunset date as an HTTP-date (RFC 7231) string, e.g. `Wed, 01 Jul 2026 00:00:00 GMT`.", "head": "eng-91", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api", "title": "ENG-91: Add deprecation headers to v1 endpoints"}, "ok": true}
